  "title": "Intellectual Property Rights Framework",
  "slug": "intellectual-property-rights-framework",
  "public": true,
  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:intellectual-property-rights-framework",
  "domain": "governance",
  "definition": "An Intellectual Property Rights Framework is the structured system of legal doctrines, statutes, treaties, and enforcement mechanisms that grant creators and innovators exclusive, time-limited rights over their intangible works \u2014 encompassing copyright, patent, trade mark, and trade secret regimes. The framework defines conditions of ownership, permissible use, licensing, and transfer of rights, balancing the incentive to create against the public interest in open knowledge. In the context of AI, spatial computing, and distributed digital environments, the framework is under active re-negotiation as autonomous generation, data-intensive training, and cross-jurisdictional virtual economies challenge foundational assumptions about authorship and originality.",
